        {
          "id": "f7d66469-7547-3be5-b961-0c278f7da809",
          "content": {
            "id": "f7d66469-7547-3be5-b961-0c278f7da809",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Bank earnings: What to expect in 2026 amid capital market changes",
            "description": "<p>Earnings season starts for major banks JPMorgan Chase (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JPM\">JPM</a>), Bank of America (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BAC\">BAC</a>), Citigroup (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/C\">C</a>), Morgan Stanley (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/MS\">MS</a>), Wells Fargo (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/WFC\">WFC</a>), and Goldman Sachs (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/GS\">GS</a>) this week, all of these major financial stocks set to report fourth quarter earnings results throughout the week.</p>\n<p>RBC Capital Markets analyst Gerard Cassidy shares her outlook on the investment banking sector for 2026, referencing US real GDP (gross domestic product) forecasts.</p>\n<p>Also hear Gerard Cassidy explain why President Trump's suggested 10% cap on credit card rates would <a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/trumps-credit-card-cap-real-161227857.html\">have \"real negative repercussions\" </a>for borrowers.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:8;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "Earnings season starts for major banks JPMorgan Chase (JPM), Bank of America (BAC), Citigroup (C), Morgan Stanley (MS), Wells Fargo (WFC), and Goldman Sachs (GS) this week, all of these major financial stocks set to report fourth quarter earnings results throughout the week. RBC Capital Markets analyst Gerard Cassidy shares her outlook on the investment banking sector for 2026, referencing US real GDP (gross domestic product) forecasts. Also hear Gerard Cassidy explain why President Trump's suggested 10% cap on credit card rates would have \"real negative repercussions\" for borrowers. To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more&nbsp;Market Catalysts.",
